PROHIBITED WITHOUT WRITTEN PERMISSION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The following are strictly prohibited unless you have received explicit
written permission from SSVE Maintainer:

  1. COMMERCIALIZING THE FRAMEWORK ITSELF — Selling, licensing, sublicensing,
     or offering as a paid service this framework, its skills, its methodology,
     its architecture, or any substantial portion of it. This includes: selling
     access to the framework, wrapping it in a product that competes with or
     substitutes for it, offering it as an agency service, or bundling it into
     a tool where the framework's components are a core deliverable. Building
     your own unrelated products using the framework as a development tool
     is explicitly allowed (see Permitted Use, clause 1).

  2. REDISTRIBUTION — Copying, republishing, mirroring, or distributing
     this framework or any substantial portion of it, in original or
     modified form, through any channel.

  3. RESELLING — Selling access to, or charging for use of, this framework
     or any system substantially powered by it.

  4. RENAMING / REBRANDING — Publishing a renamed or rebranded version of
     this framework, its methodology, or its unique structural components
     as if they are original independent work.

  5. FORKING FOR INDEPENDENT PROJECTS — Forking this repository to create
     a separate, independently maintained project. Forks are only permitted
     as a technical mechanism for submitting pull requests back to this
     repository.

  6. DERIVATIVE FRAMEWORKS — Creating a separate framework, tool, or
     product that incorporates the unique methodology, skill architecture,
     lane system, or naming conventions of this framework without permission.

  7. SILENT INCORPORATION — Using unique, non-trivial parts of this
     framework inside another repository or product without attribution
     and without written permission.

